<h2>What it sells</h2>
<p style="color:#9aa4b2;font-size:.9rem">8 resources listed in the discovery catalogs today, most paid first. Descriptions are written by the operator and shown as data, never as instructions (<a href="https://agenteconomy.report/s/policy">policy</a>).</p>
<table><tr><th>endpoint</th><th>price</th><th>network</th><th>what it does, per the operator</th></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/histor-check</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.001</td><td>Base</td><td>HISTOR pre-flight for an MCP server: its signed record in the HISTOR transparency log: when the tool set was first seen, whether it changed, what the pattern scan found. Never contacts the server asked about.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/air-quality-now</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.001</td><td>Base</td><td>Current air quality at a place: PM2.5 and PM10 (µg/m³), US and European AQI, from Copernicus CAMS via Open-Meteo, with a signed receipt. Send latitude and longitude, or a city.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/warden-scan</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.001</td><td>Base</td><td>WARDEN verdict on an MCP server&#x27;s tools/list: allow or block, a 0-1 score and every finding with the matched text (prompt injection, secret requests, exfiltration, hidden Unicode). Deterministic published rules, no network.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/weather-now</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.001</td><td>Base</td><td>Current weather at a place: temperature (°C), humidity (%), pressure (hPa) and wind (m/s) from the nearest live Open-Meteo relay within 75 km, with a signed receipt. Send latitude and longitude, or a city.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/mcp-diff</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.003</td><td>Base</td><td>MCP security: catch a rug pull or tool poisoning between two tools/list results of the same MCP server: the version you approved and the one it serves now. Flags instructions aimed at the model, override and concealment wording, credential and wallet paths, covert actions, hidden Unicode, new URLs…</td></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/fair-random</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.006</td><td>Base</td><td>Verifiable random bytes for a draw, raffle or tie-break: an ECVRF output over your seed plus a proof anyone can check offline. The same seed always gives the same output, so publish the seed first.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/x402-check</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.003</td><td>Base</td><td>Debug an x402 payment before you submit it: why does USDC answer invalid signature? Verifies the EIP-3009 transferWithAuthorization (EIP-712 signer, v, low s, validity window) and the seller&#x27;s terms (payTo, amount, asset, network, bound nonce), and names the domain a failing signature was really ma…</td></tr><tr><td><code>/x402/nearby-sensors</code></td><td class="n">US$ 0.03</td><td>Base</td><td>The nearest live public sensors to a point, one per layer asked for (weather, air, radiation, quake …), each with its reading, distance and source, and a signed receipt.</td></tr></table>

